.TH TULPAR-HISTORY 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.1.0" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar-history, tulpar-audit, tulpar-log \- show past install/remove operations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar history
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tulpar audit
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tulpar log
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tulpar a
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tulpar \-a
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the recorded history of install, remove, and rollback
operations from the package database's audit journal, in
chronological order.
.B history
,
.B audit
, and
.B log
are equivalent spellings of the same command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dest " " \fIpath\fR
Read the journal of an alternate root.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Print the history as a JSON array instead of human-readable text.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar (1),
.BR tulpar-verify (1)
